<s>\begin{slide}

%%%%** Section 2 
\section{FreeRTOS   Tasks and Calls}

\subsection{Sleep}

{\tt void Sleep(int timems)}

Code for {\tt Sleep()}
\begin{verbatim}
void Sleep( int timems )
{
  vTaskDelay( timems / portTICK_RATE_MS );
}
\end{verbatim}

Thus {\tt Sleep()} is just a new name for {\tt vTaskDelay()}.



<s>\end{slide}
<s>\begin{slide}
\subsection{Why Sleep is important.}

In a priority based scheduler, need to allow lower priority tasks to run:

\begin{verbatim}
void ExampleTask(void *p)
{
      while( 1 )
  {
    Led_SetState( 0 ); // turn the LED off
    Sleep( 900 ); // leave it off for 900 milliseconds
    Led_SetState( 1 ); // turn the LED on
    Sleep( 10 ); // leave it on for 10 milliseconds
  }
}
\end{verbatim}

Sleep does {\bf two} things:

\begin{enumerate}
  \item Makes the LED flash with proper on and off durations. 
  \item Allows FreeRTOS to give CPU to {\bf other} tasks.
\end{enumerate}


%%%%** Section 2.1
\subsection{Task Priorities}
 
\{0-7\}

High priority numbers have the  highest priority. 
 
